# Project Conventions

## Stack

- TypeScript 5.9, React 19, Next.js 16 (App Router)
- SCSS Modules for styling, clsx for class composition
- next-intl for i18n (messages in `messages/{en,fr,es}.json`)
- lucide-react for icons (via `components/Icon`)
- Contentful as CMS (data fetched in server components)
- amazon-cognito-identity-js for auth

## Architecture

- **Server Components** for data fetching (`app/[lang]/` pages, layout)
- **Client Components** marked with `"use client"` for interactivity
- Component files: `components/ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx` + `.module.scss`
- Utils in `utils/` — pure functions, no React imports
- Hooks in `hooks/` — client-side only

## Code Style

- Never use `!important` in CSS
- Never add comments that just narrate what code does
- Use `clsx` (imported as `cx` or `clsx`) for conditional class names
- Translations: use `useTranslations()` from next-intl, keys in `messages/*.json`
- All three locale files (en, fr, es) must stay in sync when adding translations
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones

## Contentful Data

- Menu data: `extractMenuColumns()` from `utils/menuHelpers.ts`
- Links: `contentfulItemToLink()` from `utils/linkHelpers.ts`
- Pages: `getPageBySlug()` from `utils/content.ts`
- Locales: `getContentfulLocale()` maps app locale to Contentful locale

## Component Patterns

- Icons: `<Icon name="IconName" size={24} />` — name is PascalCase or kebab-case
- Buttons: `<Button variant="primary" size="sm" />` — variants: primary, secondary, toggle, danger, warning, link
- Sections: wrap in `<SectionConnector>` with section props from Contentful
- Headings: `<Heading as="h1" size="h1">` — `as` is semantic, `size` is visual

## Caching & Revalidation

- Pages that display events (`app/events/page.tsx`, `app/[[...slug]]/page.tsx`) use `revalidate = 3600` (1 hour) — homepage shows event listings
- Media and other static pages (`app/media/`) use `revalidate = 86400` (24 hours) — content rarely changes
- Keep revalidate high to stay within Contentful's free-tier API limit (100k calls/month)
- Layout fetches shared data (header, footer, nav) on every page regeneration — high TTLs prevent excessive API calls
- For immediate content updates, use the preview/draft mode or consider on-demand revalidation via Contentful webhooks
- Hosted on Netlify with `@netlify/plugin-nextjs` — do not set `publish` in `netlify.toml`

